# CODEOWNERS — source routing declaration for sensitive paths
#
# This file is ROUTING METADATA ONLY. It distinguishes three things that must
# never be conflated (issue #11793):
#
#   1. a source routing declaration        — this file;
#   2. current-head review evidence        — an independent adversarial
#      review packet over the exact reviewed head
#      (schemas/agent_review_packet.v1.schema.json, #10881/#11701);
#   3. live required-review enforcement    — branch protection / rulesets,
#      owned by the enforcement successor #11796.
#
# A CODEOWNERS pattern is not proof that review happened, and review evidence
# is never satisfied by issue labels or PR colour. The checked denominator of
# sensitive authority surfaces and their required-evidence classes lives in
# policy/review-surfaces.toml (validated by scripts/ci/validate_review_surfaces.py).
#
# Owner identity: every owner below must be platform-validated with repository
# access and recorded in [code_owner_identity] there. @EffortlessMetrics is an
# organization without a /team suffix, which GitHub cannot assign; rows were
# repaired to the validated admin user in #11793.
# See: scripts/control-plane-lock.sh for the advisory write lock.

